WEBVTT

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:03.450
<i>He's one of Solomon's pillars.</i>

00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:05.270
<i>A Great President of Hell,</i>

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:08.690
<i>ruling over 30 demon armies and 
ranked 53rd in the demon hierarchy,</i>

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:11.060
<i>a protégé of Beelzebub,</i>

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:14.260
<i>and the third candidate to 
be interim ruler, Camio.</i>

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:25.040
Jellied eels again?

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:26.750
How many times have we had it this month?

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:29.590
I'm not much of a fan, either.

00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:33.010
If you don't care for eel, 
why not have candy instead?

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.840
Are you supposed to be some little princess?!

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:41.200
I've given up on enjoying human food.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:43.990
If I think of it as a sort of 
training, it's just tolerable.

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:47.130
Don't act like you've adjusted!

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:48.060
Whoa...

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:49.390
Head Boy!

00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:50.730
My apologies.

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:51.610
It's fine.

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:53.090
Greetings.

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:55.400
Hello.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:03.410
He's a Great President of Hell, 
as well as our Head Boy.

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:05.870
He does have a sort of 
air about him, doesn't he?

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:10.650
If he's also a candidate for interim ruler, 
shouldn't you two consider him a rival?

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:13.010
You seemed quite at ease, 
from those casual greetings.

00:01:13.480 --> 00:01:16.300
Grace and decorum are 
very important to demons.

00:01:16.490 --> 00:01:17.930
Though, were I ordered to do so,

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:20.640
I'd have no issue with 
settling things by force.

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:24.950
Oh boy, our school would be the 
battlefield for a huge magical war!

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:26.600
Don't even joke about that!

00:01:27.190 --> 00:01:32.480
William, we're keeping up this 
human facade for your benefit.

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:33.480
Show some gratitude.

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:35.320
Huh? Excuse me?

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:38.280
If your meathead buddies on the 
rugby team are any indication,

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:39.660
you're getting far too comfortable.

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:40.990
Shows how low-level you are.

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:43.880
Well, I don't know if you 
call them a fan club or what,

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:46.330
but I wouldn't get cocky just because 
a few boys fawn over you.

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:47.470
What did you say?

00:01:47.470 --> 00:01:49.260
You want me to say it again?

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:52.340
What a childish argument...

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:54.000
William?

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:58.300
It's time for the results from 
our last exam to be posted.

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:01.890
My greatest concerns are my 
pursuit of knowledge and my tuition.

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:03.970
I don't care about the power struggles of demons!

00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:43.360
Top of the class again, William.

00:03:43.570 --> 00:03:45.000
Well done.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:48.330
It's so predictable at this point, 
I'm not even excited.

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:51.540
Fifty-second... That's a solid showing.

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:54.030
You must have cheated.

00:03:54.030 --> 00:03:55.470
I did it on my own merit.

00:03:55.470 --> 00:03:57.780
Your human academics are easily mastered.

00:03:57.780 --> 00:03:59.720
What was that?! You lie!

00:03:59.720 --> 00:04:01.260
Look at Sytry's rank!

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:04.260
This is what you demons' merit is worth.

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:08.790
Have you not heard of long-term planning?

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:10.660
Many will lend their hands to help

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:13.210
a struggling student who happens to be beautiful.

00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:17.860
In other words, I get plenty of academic 
assistance and sweets, all with no effort.

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:18.980
Take your exams seriously!

00:04:19.550 --> 00:04:22.280
And of course, the Head Boy's got 
the top score in the school.

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:26.300
He's been on top since he 
started school. It's incredible.

00:04:27.710 --> 00:04:31.690
Someone who's been around for hundreds 
of years is bound to be quite learned.

00:04:31.690 --> 00:04:36.130
And Isaac, how long do you intend to 
remain in the lower fifth year, anyway?

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:39.420
Yeah, I wonder when I'll make 
it to the upper fifth year...

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:45.180
I'm pretty knowledgeable when it 
comes to demons, fairies, and tea...

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:47.560
Why tea?

00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:49.300
Oh, I've never told you?

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:52.110
My family is in the trade business.

00:04:52.110 --> 00:04:54.840
They deal in teas and spices from India.

00:04:55.270 --> 00:04:56.730
I had no idea.

00:04:57.510 --> 00:05:01.640
The brand that my father founded, 
Morton, is quite well-known.

00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:04.450
Lately, he's been doing business 
with the royal family!

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:09.680
And when he so generously provides 
his son with a top-tier education,

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:11.270
you let it go to waste.

00:05:11.270 --> 00:05:13.410
Come on...

00:05:18.370 --> 00:05:19.710
The Headmaster.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:22.710
I bet he's come to 
congratulate the Head Boy.

00:05:23.110 --> 00:05:24.270
I see.

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:33.470
I believe Twining would be 
best suited to handle this.

00:05:44.270 --> 00:05:46.420
Ceylon Silver Needle.

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:49.990
The Headmaster's House has excellent tea!

00:05:50.860 --> 00:05:52.950
And this room is so luxurious.

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:54.850
It's a class apart from Jacob House.

00:05:56.520 --> 00:05:58.980
The cream is so rich...

00:05:59.490 --> 00:06:01.810
It's not quite on the level 
of Baphomet's cooking,

00:06:01.810 --> 00:06:05.460
but it's the first decent meal I've 
had since coming to this school.

00:06:05.750 --> 00:06:09.630
Anyway, Head Boy, what's this task 
you were trying to force on me?

00:06:10.060 --> 00:06:15.180
I've no intention of negotiating 
with you over afternoon tea.

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:17.850
This is simple hospitality.

00:06:18.340 --> 00:06:21.270
The issue at hand is the 
construction of a new building.

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:23.070
New building?

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:24.490
Yes.

00:06:24.490 --> 00:06:27.580
They're going to tear down the water 
mill behind the Headmaster's House

00:06:27.580 --> 00:06:29.320
and put a new classroom building there.

00:06:30.020 --> 00:06:33.520
He's been soliciting for donations everywhere,

00:06:33.520 --> 00:06:35.680
and the academy chairman is coming this week

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:37.270
to check on the Headmaster's progress.

00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:40.680
He's very keen to rake in some big donations.

00:06:40.680 --> 00:06:43.040
So what's the problem?

00:06:43.760 --> 00:06:44.730
Well...

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:48.950
Recently we've had some problems 
with discipline in our dormitory.

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:50.510
Discipline?

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:53.830
Yes, people singing and making 
a ruckus late at night,

00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:56.070
breaking curfew, and so on.

00:06:56.760 --> 00:07:01.250
As you know, all the students in this dorm
are handpicked as the best of the best.

00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:04.860
I'm impressed you can say that so unabashedly.

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:06.910
What can I say? It's true.

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:12.640
At any rate, if the chairman catches 
wind of these rule breakers,

00:07:12.640 --> 00:07:15.680
it'll reflect poorly on the Headmaster
and possibly cost him donations.

00:07:16.140 --> 00:07:19.380
I need you to sniff out the problem students

00:07:19.380 --> 00:07:21.110
and stop them before the chairman arrives.

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:23.330
I understand the problem now.

00:07:23.550 --> 00:07:26.830
But why must it be me?

00:07:26.830 --> 00:07:30.020
The Headmaster's House is your 
responsibility as the Head Boy.

00:07:30.590 --> 00:07:32.090
Twining.

00:07:32.090 --> 00:07:34.010
I asked because it would be to your benefit.

00:07:34.240 --> 00:07:35.230
What?

00:07:35.230 --> 00:07:38.380
Do you think I'm some freelance helper-for-hire?

00:07:38.380 --> 00:07:40.800
You are struggling with your tuition, are you not?

00:07:41.680 --> 00:07:45.860
Being in the Headmaster's good 
graces can only help you.

00:07:45.860 --> 00:07:48.410
Maybe, just maybe, 
you'll be the youngest boy ever

00:07:48.410 --> 00:07:49.960
to be admitted into the Headmaster's House.

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:54.520
<i>Splendid work, Twining. Many thanks.</i>

00:07:54.520 --> 00:08:00.160
<i>Chairman, this is our academy's 
brightest and most promising student.</i>

00:08:00.510 --> 00:08:02.440
<i>Magnificent!</i>

00:08:02.440 --> 00:08:04.630
<i>I insist he be exempted from tuition.</i>

00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:06.140
<i>Give him a full scholarship,</i>

00:08:06.140 --> 00:08:08.550
<i>and start lining up a job 
for when he graduates!</i>

00:08:09.260 --> 00:08:11.160
<i>Thank you, sir!</i>

00:08:14.940 --> 00:08:16.650
Head Boy, you have my thanks!

00:08:16.650 --> 00:08:18.220
Long live the Head Boy!

00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:20.140
I'll leave you to it, then.

00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:22.370
Where are you going?

00:08:22.370 --> 00:08:23.480
The library.

00:08:23.680 --> 00:08:25.550
There's a book I've been wanting to read.

00:08:31.010 --> 00:08:32.350
Did he...

00:08:32.350 --> 00:08:34.650
He just pawned the job off on him.

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:36.990
Wh-What was that?!

00:08:36.990 --> 00:08:39.580
You call yourselves Grand Dukes 
and Archdukes and whatnot,

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:41.810
but you're just average, ordinary demons!

00:08:41.810 --> 00:08:43.540
Nowhere near the level of a Great President!

00:08:43.850 --> 00:08:45.290
You'll pay for that one.

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:48.250
I already said I'd take care of your tuition!

00:08:48.250 --> 00:08:49.270
Stuff it.

00:08:49.700 --> 00:08:52.060
I don't want to be in debt to either of you!

00:08:55.220 --> 00:08:58.600
You'd better not be thinking 
about electing Camio.

00:08:59.890 --> 00:09:02.520
I am not. I don't intend to elect anyone.

00:09:02.820 --> 00:09:04.320
Then do what you want.

00:09:04.320 --> 00:09:05.950
Just don't come crying to me afterwards!

00:09:05.950 --> 00:09:07.440
Not in this lifetime!

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:17.570
The Headmaster's House is here.

00:09:18.350 --> 00:09:19.930
Since there's no fencing,

00:09:19.930 --> 00:09:24.080
it'll be difficult to catch the culprits
if they run off into the woods.

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:27.290
I guess all we can do is seize them on the spot.

00:09:28.850 --> 00:09:32.250
Me, a member of the renowned Twining family,

00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:33.260
forced into a stakeout...

00:09:33.580 --> 00:09:35.720
You'd better pray it doesn't rain tonight.

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:39.170
Oh, shut up! Why are you here, anyway?!

00:09:39.630 --> 00:09:41.220
It sounded fun.

00:09:42.440 --> 00:09:45.790
You demons never take anything seriously...

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:50.610
Whether we go with a 
stakeout or an ambush,

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:53.000
we'll want to check the area first.

00:09:53.850 --> 00:09:56.180
Walking through the woods at night...

00:09:56.180 --> 00:09:58.570
What if a ghost comes after us?

00:09:59.270 --> 00:10:00.890
And demons don't bother you?

00:10:00.890 --> 00:10:03.460
They're a completely different story.

00:10:03.460 --> 00:10:04.910
You're not making sense!

00:10:04.910 --> 00:10:07.090
Ghosts are scary!

00:10:07.090 --> 00:10:08.960
We might get cursed or possessed!

00:10:09.560 --> 00:10:12.150
Listen, your so-called 
"ghosts" are almost always

00:10:12.150 --> 00:10:16.180
visual or auditory hallucinations caused by 
electromagnetic waves of high or low frequencies.

00:10:16.640 --> 00:10:18.360
The brain merely misreads the subtle lines

00:10:18.360 --> 00:10:20.180
between the bands of frequency that

00:10:20.180 --> 00:10:22.100
the senses of sight and sound can detect.

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:24.290
B-But demons are real.

00:10:24.290 --> 00:10:25.790
They're made of atoms.

00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:30.010
Still, ghosts give me the—

00:10:30.950 --> 00:10:32.160
What's that?!

00:10:32.990 --> 00:10:34.890
I hear something.

00:10:34.890 --> 00:10:37.130
Is that the singing the 
Head Boy mentioned?

00:10:37.890 --> 00:10:38.540
This way.

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:40.640
Don't go!

00:10:40.640 --> 00:10:42.550
Stay there if you're scared!

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:45.340
That's not any better!

00:10:49.760 --> 00:10:51.550
No one's here...

00:10:51.550 --> 00:10:53.100
This is the old water mill?

00:10:54.090 --> 00:10:57.130
The Head Boy said they were 
going to tear it down...

00:10:57.560 --> 00:10:59.510
But it looks like they haven't 
started construction yet.

00:11:01.690 --> 00:11:04.930
Let's go back! No one's here anyway...

00:11:05.190 --> 00:11:06.970
Fine, fine.

00:11:06.970 --> 00:11:10.310
No one's going to show up 
with you making such a fuss.

00:11:10.560 --> 00:11:12.080
Let's go back for today.

00:11:12.080 --> 00:11:13.350
Thank goodness...

00:11:13.940 --> 00:11:15.900
Rule breakers, huh?

00:11:26.160 --> 00:11:29.580
Duke Dantalion has returned!

00:11:30.550 --> 00:11:33.290
Every single time, you guys do this!

00:11:33.290 --> 00:11:34.880
You don't have to tell me!

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:37.000
I can feel Dantalion's presence 
the instant he arrives!

00:11:37.700 --> 00:11:38.960
Hello, Lamia.

00:11:42.570 --> 00:11:46.320
No kiss hello for the fiancée 
you haven't seen in so long?

00:11:47.120 --> 00:11:48.780
Fiancée? Whose?

00:11:49.320 --> 00:11:50.350
Yours!

00:11:51.030 --> 00:11:52.180
Who's my fiancée?

00:11:52.180 --> 00:11:54.410
M-Me, of course!

00:11:54.410 --> 00:11:58.030
You promised to marry me! 
I won't let you tell me you forgot!

00:11:58.870 --> 00:12:00.150
Where's Astaroth?

00:12:00.150 --> 00:12:03.610
Hey, don't go in there! Lady Astaroth is...

00:12:08.430 --> 00:12:09.560
Dantalion?

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:14.040
My master hopes to find you well.

00:12:15.330 --> 00:12:16.500
Oh, stop.

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:19.670
Hearing you speak so politely 
gives me the creeps.

00:12:20.280 --> 00:12:22.770
Lady Astaroth, please put some clothes on!

00:12:23.740 --> 00:12:27.640
It's just Dantalion. 
What need is there for modesty?

00:12:28.260 --> 00:12:32.020
Now tell me, what of the third candidate?

00:12:32.830 --> 00:12:33.980
I can't stand him.

00:12:35.570 --> 00:12:36.890
I figured.

00:12:37.260 --> 00:12:39.700
You'll need to take a different 
approach if you're dealing

00:12:39.700 --> 00:12:41.940
with someone Beelzebub's 
taken under his wing.

00:12:42.170 --> 00:12:43.430
I'll say.

00:12:43.430 --> 00:12:46.530
I have no idea what he's thinking.

00:12:47.770 --> 00:12:51.290
He doesn't seem too enthusiastic 
about winning the throne.

00:12:52.190 --> 00:12:54.020
It may be he's overconfident.

00:12:55.090 --> 00:12:59.460
Camio's of a much higher 
class than you or Sytry.

00:13:00.900 --> 00:13:02.420
You're speaking of his lineage?

00:13:04.440 --> 00:13:05.910
Who cares about lineage?

00:13:05.910 --> 00:13:08.010
That's got nothing to do 
with the person himself!

00:13:09.150 --> 00:13:11.090
It just doesn't work that way.

00:13:11.090 --> 00:13:13.430
And as if that weren't bad 
enough, we're Nephilim.

00:13:15.170 --> 00:13:16.020
However...

00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:20.360
Camio's not who you should 
be concerned about.

00:13:23.150 --> 00:13:24.820
Dantalion, don't look!

00:13:26.030 --> 00:13:29.590
There's someone much more 
dangerous at the Elector's side.

00:13:32.690 --> 00:13:35.330
The chairman's visiting 
at the end of the month,

00:13:35.690 --> 00:13:37.790
so I need to wrap things up this week.

00:13:39.120 --> 00:13:41.220
And what are you doing here, Isaac?!

00:13:41.220 --> 00:13:42.710
Let me sleep with you.

00:13:43.450 --> 00:13:46.470
What if the ghosts get into the dorm?

00:13:46.690 --> 00:13:48.360
But what's this for?

00:13:48.360 --> 00:13:51.430
Don't take it off! It's to ward off spirits!

00:13:51.770 --> 00:13:54.890
I told you, ghosts are just...

00:13:59.360 --> 00:14:00.950
Goodnight, William.

00:14:00.950 --> 00:14:01.820
Don't go to sleep!

00:14:15.440 --> 00:14:17.920
You stink and you're loud! 
I can't sleep like this!

00:14:18.350 --> 00:14:24.230
Barley, wheat, corn, and ash...

00:14:24.230 --> 00:14:29.480
Grind and grind and grind, 
grind and grind...

00:14:30.150 --> 00:14:32.370
Wake up! Wake up, Isaac!

00:14:30.150 --> 00:14:38.190
Bitter and mad, lonely and sad, 
it's not fair, it's not fair...

00:14:34.320 --> 00:14:36.090
You hear that?

00:14:37.190 --> 00:14:38.190
What?

00:14:38.490 --> 00:14:40.620
It's that odd song again.

00:14:41.550 --> 00:14:42.650
Again?

00:14:42.900 --> 00:14:47.940
Grind and grind and grind, 
grind and grind...

00:14:48.410 --> 00:14:49.460
Where're you going?

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:51.880
Grind and grind...

00:14:49.460 --> 00:14:51.020
To catch these troublemakers!

00:14:51.680 --> 00:14:54.120
Wait, don't leave me alone!

00:14:51.880 --> 00:14:57.860
It won't turn, it won't move...

00:14:57.860 --> 00:15:03.420
It's so sad, it's not fair...

00:15:02.530 --> 00:15:03.420
Who's there?!

00:15:07.040 --> 00:15:07.750
Freeze!

00:15:08.790 --> 00:15:09.590
Wait up!

00:15:12.190 --> 00:15:16.560
No student's going to be up singing at 
a water mill in the middle of the night!

00:15:16.560 --> 00:15:18.470
It has to be a ghost.

00:15:18.470 --> 00:15:21.620
No, it could be a student 
who's mad at the Headmaster

00:15:21.620 --> 00:15:23.970
and wants to spread bad rumors.

00:15:23.970 --> 00:15:26.820
Or maybe just a very elaborate prank.

00:15:27.940 --> 00:15:31.210
You're very insistent that it's a 
human doing this, huh, William?

00:15:31.210 --> 00:15:33.400
Logic and evidence dictate as much.

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:35.810
Between the two,

00:15:35.810 --> 00:15:38.500
I'd rather it be a human than a ghost, but...

00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:49.300
Calm down, Isaac!

00:15:49.550 --> 00:15:51.970
Evil spirit, begone! I cast thee out!

00:15:51.970 --> 00:15:54.500
Amen! Amen!

00:15:58.650 --> 00:16:00.480
You're supposed to be the occult expert!

00:16:01.300 --> 00:16:03.230
I told you, ghosts are different!

00:16:04.670 --> 00:16:05.900
Don't curse me!

00:16:09.910 --> 00:16:12.910
Get out here, ghost! I'll hear you out.

00:16:14.820 --> 00:16:18.170
You have the right to an attorney.

00:16:18.170 --> 00:16:21.830
If you prefer to remain 
silent, please inform me.

00:16:22.130 --> 00:16:23.950
You're incredible, William.

00:16:23.950 --> 00:16:26.670
No one else would read a ghost his rights!

00:16:30.190 --> 00:16:36.360
Bitter and mad, lonely and sad,

00:16:36.360 --> 00:16:38.700
it's not fair, it's not fair...

00:16:38.700 --> 00:16:39.980
So it was you.

00:16:42.020 --> 00:16:44.480
The defendant will make his statements first.

00:16:44.810 --> 00:16:45.910
What is your name?

00:16:45.910 --> 00:16:49.070
Barley and wheat, grind—

00:16:49.070 --> 00:16:53.070
I asked for your name, 
not that song of yours!

00:16:53.070 --> 00:16:56.370
William Twining, prefect of Jacob House,

00:16:56.370 --> 00:16:58.590
is speaking to you as an equal.

00:16:58.590 --> 00:17:00.120
How dare you be flippant with me?

00:17:00.590 --> 00:17:01.890
And now a lecture!

00:17:01.890 --> 00:17:03.580
You're so dependable, William!

00:17:05.470 --> 00:17:11.550
You say you lived here for many years, 
milling grain with this water mill?

00:17:14.010 --> 00:17:17.160
But lately, there's been no work for you,

00:17:17.160 --> 00:17:20.570
and on top of that, you were crushed 
when you heard it would be torn down.

00:17:20.570 --> 00:17:22.730
You tried to petition the Headmaster's House

00:17:22.730 --> 00:17:25.350
to call off the demolition numerous times,

00:17:25.350 --> 00:17:27.240
but it fell on deaf ears.

00:17:27.790 --> 00:17:30.730
And now you're even bringing 
your petitions to Jacob House.

00:17:36.210 --> 00:17:40.240
But the decision to start construction 
on the new building is already made.

00:17:40.240 --> 00:17:43.290
And a school doesn't need a water mill.

00:17:47.480 --> 00:17:50.490
Let it go and find a new career.

00:17:51.660 --> 00:17:53.090
No, no!

00:17:53.750 --> 00:17:55.480
Face reality!

00:17:56.490 --> 00:17:58.530
Telling him that won't do any good.

00:17:59.660 --> 00:18:01.470
That's a killmoulis.

00:18:01.760 --> 00:18:03.130
Killmoulis?

00:18:03.130 --> 00:18:05.440
You mean like the fairies?

00:18:05.440 --> 00:18:07.980
Isaac, you've heard of them?

00:18:08.480 --> 00:18:12.440
Killmoulis are fairies that live 
in water mills in Scotland!

00:18:12.760 --> 00:18:15.340
Then why didn't you recognize him as one?!

00:18:15.800 --> 00:18:19.330
Because he doesn't look anything 
like the picture in the book!

00:18:21.210 --> 00:18:26.940
Well, fairy or not, what's a creature 
from that far north doing here?

00:18:28.440 --> 00:18:30.850
Actually, I suppose water mills

00:18:30.850 --> 00:18:34.630
are becoming obsolete in our modern 
society with its industrial advances.

00:18:34.630 --> 00:18:35.800
They're relics of the past.

00:18:36.400 --> 00:18:39.850
He must've been looking for a 
mill that was still operating,

00:18:39.850 --> 00:18:42.230
and made his way south.

00:18:42.810 --> 00:18:46.740
If a killmoulis doesn't have 
grain to mill, he dies.

00:18:47.950 --> 00:18:49.480
You've had it rough.

00:18:52.940 --> 00:18:56.260
But the book said, if they don't have grain,

00:18:56.260 --> 00:19:00.200
killmoulis will grind up whatever 
they can get their hands on.

00:19:00.550 --> 00:19:03.410
So you were going to start 
milling human beings?!

00:19:07.800 --> 00:19:12.100
Relax, he's just a minor little goblin.

00:19:12.940 --> 00:19:14.890
Just say, "Listen, old killmoulis,"

00:19:14.890 --> 00:19:16.630
and he'll do whatever you say.

00:19:16.630 --> 00:19:18.080
He will?

00:19:18.080 --> 00:19:19.470
Then let me...

00:19:20.100 --> 00:19:21.090
Hey, you.

00:19:22.280 --> 00:19:24.810
You just need something 
to grind up, right?

00:19:36.480 --> 00:19:38.760
I guess that settles that.

00:19:38.760 --> 00:19:40.950
You're a genius, William.

00:19:41.410 --> 00:19:45.910
No one else would've thought to 
send the killmoulis to India.

00:19:46.410 --> 00:19:50.120
He's grinding spices to his heart's 
content in the factory now.

00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:55.540
My father is thrilled! He's been saying, 
"That little old man is some worker! Amazing!"

00:19:57.070 --> 00:19:58.050
Oh?

00:19:58.780 --> 00:19:59.890
Chairman.

00:20:00.720 --> 00:20:03.450
This is the boy I was telling you about.

00:20:05.590 --> 00:20:08.090
<i>The chairman's come to my aid at last!</i>

00:20:08.670 --> 00:20:13.300
The son of the Morton family, whose father 
made a generous donation to our school.

00:20:13.300 --> 00:20:14.850
What?!

00:20:15.410 --> 00:20:17.710
He's told me all about you!

00:20:17.710 --> 00:20:19.150
H-Hello, sir...

00:20:19.420 --> 00:20:24.510
He called it a token of his gratitude 
for the exceptional hired help

00:20:24.510 --> 00:20:26.740
that he recently received from this school.

00:20:27.250 --> 00:20:29.930
Give my regards to your father!

00:20:29.930 --> 00:20:31.360
Y-Yes, sir...

00:20:40.820 --> 00:20:46.650
I'll never trust a demon again!

00:21:11.990 --> 00:21:13.350
You again?

00:21:15.530 --> 00:21:18.330
How long are you going to continue 
clinging to the Young Master?

00:21:20.140 --> 00:21:23.840
So, you became a priest just 
to follow after William.

00:21:26.210 --> 00:21:28.230
I've been wanting to know...

00:21:29.430 --> 00:21:30.400
Yes?

00:21:31.790 --> 00:21:34.630
Who are you, really?

00:21:37.480 --> 00:21:40.210
I am but a simple house steward.

00:21:41.100 --> 00:21:44.290
As for being a priest, 
I studied theology in college.

00:21:45.000 --> 00:21:47.830
Then call upon the Hand of God.

00:21:48.250 --> 00:21:50.940
If you're really a member of the 
Church, it should be trivial.

00:21:55.720 --> 00:21:58.760
You're hiding something, too, aren't you?

00:22:00.490 --> 00:22:03.090
I'll rip that mask off soon enough,

00:22:03.090 --> 00:22:04.750
but today, I just came to say hello.

00:22:06.270 --> 00:22:08.540
Let's go, Amon, Mamon!

00:22:08.540 --> 00:22:09.430
Sir!

00:23:40.890 --> 00:23:43.480
Hi, everyone! How are you? It's Isaac!

00:23:43.480 --> 00:23:46.980
If you spot any demons or 
fairies, be sure to let me know!

00:23:46.980 --> 00:23:49.480
I'll ship you some of our tea in return!

00:23:50.090 --> 00:23:52.740
I'd like to eat a cake made by you.

00:23:52.740 --> 00:23:54.750
I wonder what it will taste like?
